@startuml
title UC6 - Explore Story - Test Cases

map "TC-UC6-01: Move between locations" as TC1 {
  Test Case Number => TC-UC6-01
  Test Case Name => Move forward, backward, and boundary check between cities
  Description => Verify player can navigate between locations and system displays current city name
  Preconditions => 1. Player is logged in \n 2. Player has a starter Pokemon
  Test Case Input => Input 1: Select "Move Forward" (not at last location) \n Input 2: Select "Move Backward" (not at first location) \n Input 3: Select "Move Backward" at first location of Phase 1 \n Input 4: Select "Move Forward" at last location of final Phase
  Expected Output => 1. "You moved forward to the next area." or "You advanced to a new Phase of your journey!" \n 2. "You returned to the previous area." or "You traveled back to the previous Phase." \n 3. "You are already at the beginning of your journey." (location unchanged) \n 4. "You cannot go any further in this direction." (location unchanged) \n All cases: Screen shows "CURRENT LOCATION: [ {CityName} ]"
  Steps => 1. Select Continue Story from Main Menu \n 2. Verify "CURRENT LOCATION: [ {CityName} ]" displayed \n 3. Test each input scenario \n 4. Verify corresponding movement message displayed \n 5. Verify city name header updated (or unchanged for boundary) \n 6. Verify location's NPCs and facilities loaded correctly
  Default Value Preserving => Player CurrentLocation updated in GameSession (unchanged for boundary cases)
}

map "TC-UC6-02: Explore wild area" as TC2 {
  Test Case Number => TC-UC6-02
  Test Case Name => Explore wild area with different outcomes
  Description => Verify wild area exploration handles encounter, no encounter, and fainted team scenarios
  Preconditions => 1. Player is at a location with wild Pokemon
  Test Case Input => Input 1: Select "Explore Wild Area" with healthy team (encounter triggered - 60% chance) \n Input 2: Select "Explore Wild Area" with healthy team (no encounter - 40% chance) \n Input 3: Select "Explore Wild Area" with all Pokemon fainted
  Expected Output => 1. "You walk into the tall grass..." then "A wild {PokemonName} jumped out of the tall grass!" → battle begins (UC2) \n 2. "You walk into the tall grass..." then "You searched the grass but only found peace and quiet." Possibly "[!] You found a {ItemName}!" → return to story screen \n 3. "It's too dangerous! All your Pokemon have fainted. Go to the Center!" → no encounter, return to story screen
  Steps => 1. From story screen, select "Explore Wild Area" \n 2. System calls StoryService.ExploreWildArea() \n 3. Verify correct message displayed based on outcome \n 4. Verify battle initiated (Input 1) or return to story screen (Input 2, 3)
  Default Value Preserving => 1. Battle outcome handled by UC2 \n 2. Item may be added to inventory \n 3. No changes
}

@enduml
